# A grammar with no `name!` start symbol parses from its first rule: the
# generated parser has a parse method for it (or generation fails with a
# located error; then turn this into a rejection test).
#
# Today: generation succeeds and builds tables for the first rule, but the
# `Start` enum is empty and the parser has no parse method, so nothing can
# be parsed (the test driver fails to compile: "parser has no parse* start
# method"). Found while documenting start symbols.

@lexer
tokens
    ident
    eof
    err
[a-z]+                                      → ident
.                                           → err

@parser
@lang = "no_start_symbol"

top  = IDENT+                               → (top ...1)
